d](/?term=%22Cytometry+A%22%5Bjour%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n-   [Search in NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Cytometry+A%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2023 Mar;103(3):184-188.\n\ndoi: 10.1002/cyto.a.24707. Epub 2022 Dec 5.\n\n# OMIP-087: Thirty-two parameter mass cytometry panel to assess human CD4 and CD8 T cell activation, memory subsets, and helper subsets\n\n[Alexis Sponaugle](/?term=Sponaugle+A&cauthor_id=36470845)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\") , [Maria Abad-Fernandez](/?term=Abad-Fernandez+M&cauthor_id=36470845)  [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\") , [Nilu Goonetilleke](/?term=Goonetilleke+N&cauthor_id=36470845)  [1](#full-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\")   [2](#full-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\")\n\nAffiliations Expand\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\n-   2 Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\n\n-   PMID: **36470845**\n-   PMCID: [PMC12244433](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12244433/)\n-   DOI: [10.1002/cyto.a.24707](https://doi.org/10.1002/cyto.a.24707)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\n# OMIP-087: Thirty-two parameter mass cytometry panel to assess human CD4 and CD8 T cell activation, memory subsets, and helper subsets\n\nAlexis Sponaugle et al. Cytometry A. 2023 Mar.\n\nShow details\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat Abstract PubMed PMID\n\nCytometry A\n\nActions\n\n-   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Cytometry+A%22%5Bjour%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n-   [Search in NLM Catalog](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/nlmcatalog?term=%22Cytometry+A%22%5BTitle+Abbreviation%5D)\n-   [Add to Search](#)\n\n. 2023 Mar;103(3):184-188.\n\ndoi: 10.1002/cyto.a.24707. Epub 2022 Dec 5.\n\n### Authors\n\n[Alexis Sponaugle](/?term=Sponaugle+A&cauthor_id=36470845)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\") , [Maria Abad-Fernandez](/?term=Abad-Fernandez+M&cauthor_id=36470845)  [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\") , [Nilu Goonetilleke](/?term=Goonetilleke+N&cauthor_id=36470845)  [1](#short-view-affiliation-1 \"Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\")   [2](#short-view-affiliation-2 \"Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\")\n\n### Affiliations\n\n-   1 Department of Microbiology and Immunology, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, USA.\n-   2 Department of Medicine, University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill, Chapel Hill, North Carolina, United States.\n\n-   PMID: **36470845**\n-   PMCID: [PMC12244433](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12244433/)\n-   DOI: [10.1002/cyto.a.24707](https://doi.org/10.1002/cyto.a.24707)\n\nItem in Clipboard\n\nFull text links Cite\n\nDisplay options\n\nDisplay options\n\nFormat AbstractPubMedPMID\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe developed a highly reproducible 32-marker mass cytometry panel able to measure all canonical immune lineages and perform detailed characterization of both CD4 and CD8 T cells in human peripheral blood mononuclear cells. In this panel, we identify six different T cell memory subsets, as well as markers of activation, cell cycling, and survival. In addition, this panel classifies all major CD4 T cell helper subsets. This panel enables detailed monitoring of CD4 and CD8 T cells in the context of infectious disease, cancer or autoimmunity with limited patient sample use. Detailed methods for standardization and optimization of the panel can be found in Supporting Information.\n\n**Keywords:** CD4 T cells; CD8 T cells; mass cytometry.\n\n© 2022 The Authors. Cytometry Part A published by Wiley Periodicals LLC on behalf of International Society for Advancement of Cytometry.\n\n[PubMed Disclaimer](/disclaimer/)\n\n## Conflict of interest statement\n\nCONFLICT OF INTEREST\n\nThe authors declare no conflict of interest.\n\n## Figures\n\n [![FIGURE 1](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/64e6/12244433/0908be532b75/nihms-2088207-f0001.gif)](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/blobs/64e6/12244433/286a6d8c73b2/nihms-2088207-f0001.jpg) \n\n**\n\nFIGURE 1\n\n**\n\nManual gating of OMIP. (A)…\n\n**\n\nFIGURE 1\n\n**\n\nManual gating of OMIP. (A) Canonical cell lineages. First, all leukocyte populations were…\n\n**FIGURE 1**\n\nManual gating of OMIP. (A) Canonical cell lineages. First, all leukocyte populations were identified as CD45+ (89Y for sample of interest and 111Cd for reference cells). Dendritic cells (DCs) were identified as CD14-CD19-CD3-HLA-DR + CD11c+, monocytes as CD3-CD19-CD14+, B cells as CD3-CD14-CD19+, and NK cells as CD3-CD14-CD19-CD16 + CD56+. CD4 T cells identified as CD3 + CD4+, CD8 T cells as CD3 + CD8+, and TCRγδ T cells as CD3 + TCRγδ+. (B) CD4 T cell memory subsets were determined using markers CD45RA, CCR7, CD28, CD95, CD99, and CCR10. Naïve T cells defined as CD45RA + CCR7 + CD28 + CD95−, stem cell memory as CD45RA + CCR7 + CD28 + CD95+, central memory as CD45RA-CCR7 + CD28 + CD95+, transitional memory as CD45RA-CCR7-CD28 + CD95+, effector memory as CD45RA-CCR7-CD28-CD95+, and terminal effectors as CD45RA + CCR7-CD28-CD95+. CD99hi and CCR10+ are enriched on memory CD4 T cells. (C) CD4 T cell helper subsets. Helper subsets were defined using OMIP-017 gating strategy using the chemokine receptors CCR4, CXCR3, CCR10, and CCR6. Treg were identified as CD25HICD127-FoxP3+ and TFH were defined as CXCR5+. (D) Activation markers CD25, Ki-67, CD38, CD57, and HLA-DR on CD4 T cells. Activation/exhaustion marker PD-1, survival marker Bcl-2 and long lived memory marker CD127 on CD4 T cells\n\n[See this image and copyright information in PMC](#)\n\n## References\n\n1.  1.  Abrahams MR, Joseph SB, Garrett N, Tyers L, Moeser M, Archin N, et al. The replication-competent HIV-1 latent reservoir is primarily established near the time of therapy initiation. Sci Transl Med. 2019;eaaw5589:11. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7233356/) - [PubMed](/31597754/)\n2.  1.  Goonetilleke N, Clutton G, Swanstrom R, Joseph SB. Blocking formation of the stable HIV reservoir: a new perspective for HIV-1 cure. Front Immunol. 2019;10:1966. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6714000/) - [PubMed](/31507594/)\n3.  1.  Brodin J, Zanini F, Thebo L, Lanz C, Bratt G, Neher RA, et al. Establishment and stability of the latent HIV-1 DNA reservoir. Elife. 2016;5:e18889. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5201419/) - [PubMed](/27855060/)\n4.  1.  Brooks K, Jones BR, Dilernia DA, Wilkins DJ, Claiborne DT, McInally S, et al. HIV-1 variants are archived throughout infection and persist in the reservoir. PLoS Pathog. 2020;16:e1008378. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7295247/) - [PubMed](/32492044/)\n5.  1.  Okoye AA, Picker LJ. CD4(+) T-cell depletion in HIV infection: mechanisms of immunological failure. Immunol Rev. 2013;254:54–64. - [PMC](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3729334/) - [PubMed](/23772614/)\n\nShow all 14 references\n\n## Publication types\n\n-   Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Research+Support%2C+Non-U.S.+Gov%27t%22%5Bpt%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Research+Support%2C+Non-U.S.+Gov%27t)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n\n## MeSH terms\n\n-   CD4-Positive T-Lymphocytes\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22CD4-Positive+T-Lymphocytes%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=CD4-Positive+T-Lymphocytes)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   CD8-Positive T-Lymphocytes\\*\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22CD8-Positive+T-Lymphocytes%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=CD8-Positive+T-Lymphocytes)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Flow Cytometry / methods\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Flow+Cytometry%2Fmethods%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Flow+Cytometry)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Humans\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Humans%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Humans)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Leukocytes, Mononuclear\\*\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Leukocytes%2C+Mononuclear%22%5BMAJR%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Leukocytes%2C+Mononuclear)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   Lymphocyte Activation\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22Lymphocyte+Activation%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=Lymphocyte+Activation)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   T-Lymphocyte Subsets\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22T-Lymphocyte+Subsets%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=T-Lymphocyte+Subsets)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n-   T-Lymphocytes, Helper-Inducer\n    \n    Actions\n    \n    -   [Search in PubMed](/?term=%22T-Lymphocytes%2C+Helper-Inducer%22%5BMeSH%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc)\n    -   [Search in MeSH](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/mesh?term=T-Lymphocytes%2C+Helper-Inducer)\n    -   [Add to Search](#)\n    \n\n## Grants and funding\n\n-   [P30 AI050410/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States](/?term=P30+AI050410%2FAI%2FNIAID+NIH+HHS%2FUnited+States%5BGrants+and+Funding%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc \"All articles for grant P30 AI050410/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States\")\n-   [P30 CA016086/CA/NCI NIH HHS/United States](/?term=P30+CA016086%2FCA%2FNCI+NIH+HHS%2FUnited+States%5BGrants+and+Funding%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc \"All articles for grant P30 CA016086/CA/NCI NIH HHS/United States\")\n-   [U01 AI131310/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States](/?term=U01+AI131310%2FAI%2FNIAID+NIH+HHS%2FUnited+States%5BGrants+and+Funding%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc \"All articles for grant U01 AI131310/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States\")\n-   [UM1 AI106701/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States](/?term=UM1+AI106701%2FAI%2FNIAID+NIH+HHS%2FUnited+States%5BGrants+and+Funding%5D&sort=date&sort_order=desc \"All articles for grant UM1 AI106701/AI/NIAID NIH HHS/United States\")\n\n## LinkOut - more resources\n\n-   ### Full Text Sources\n    \n    -   [PubMed Central](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/pmid/36470845/)\n    -   [Wiley](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cyto.a.24707)\n-   ### Research Materials\n    \n    -   [NCI CPTC Antibody Characterization Program](https://antibodies.cancer.gov/detail/CPTC-CD4-2)\n\n**Full text links** \\[x\\]\n\n [![Wiley full text link](https://cdn.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/corehtml/query/egifs/http:--media.wiley.com-assets-7388-68-wiley-free-full-text.png) Wiley](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/cyto.a.24707 \"See full text options