{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778975886745,"sessionID":"ses_1ccc91ca1ffeAz0tVsMxSuhbjd","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_1pW3QX12HRZHMlslwGX0TLXM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated the two requested human dendritic cell terms, `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`, to include CD14-negative status. I did not apply this to the broader `CL_0001056` human dendritic cell term, consistent with the maintainer note that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n*** Add File: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+## Summary\n+\n+This PR addresses issue #3163 by adding CD14-negative characterization to the two requested human dendritic cell terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0001057` myeloid dendritic cell, human\n+- `CL_0001058` plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\n+\n+The broader `CL_0001056` dendritic cell, human term was intentionally left unchanged because the issue discussion notes that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001057` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001058` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as additional definition xrefs without removing the existing `PMID:22343568` reference:\n+  - `PMID:34260151`\n+  - `PMID:36470845`\n+  - `PMID:37254600`\n+  - `PMID:38343094`\n+  - `PMID:40095400`\n+- Added logical axioms using the existing Cell Ontology pattern for lacking a plasma membrane part:\n+  - `CL_4030046 some PR_000001350` for CD14-negative status\n+- Added issue tracker annotations linking both updated terms to issue #3163.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The existing human dendritic cell terms are modeled using marker phenotype restrictions. CD14-negative status is represented logically with `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`) and `PR_000001350` for CD14, matching existing ontology patterns for absent surface markers. The change was limited to the two terms explicitly requested and supported by the issue discussion.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Reviewed imported issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked the existing term blocks for `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`.\n+- Checked the existing marker expression and lacking-expression ontology pattern.\n+- Verified the supplied PMIDs correspond to OMIP immunophenotyping references.\n+- Preserved existing references and added the requested references.\n+- Avoided modifying the broader `CL_0001056` term.\n+- Validated ontology functional syntax with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`.\n+- Checked the diff for whitespace errors with `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+- `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`: passed\n+- `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`: passed\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated the two requested human dendritic cell terms, `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`, to include CD14-negative status. I did not apply this to the broader `CL_0001056` human dendritic cell term, consistent with the maintainer note that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n\nIndex: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@\n+## Summary\n+\n+This PR addresses issue #3163 by adding CD14-negative characterization to the two requested human dendritic cell terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0001057` myeloid dendritic cell, human\n+- `CL_0001058` plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\n+\n+The broader `CL_0001056` dendritic cell, human term was intentionally left unchanged because the issue discussion notes that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001057` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001058` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as additional definition xrefs without removing the existing `PMID:22343568` reference:\n+  - `PMID:34260151`\n+  - `PMID:36470845`\n+  - `PMID:37254600`\n+  - `PMID:38343094`\n+  - `PMID:40095400`\n+- Added logical axioms using the existing Cell Ontology pattern for lacking a plasma membrane part:\n+  - `CL_4030046 some PR_000001350` for CD14-negative status\n+- Added issue tracker annotations linking both updated terms to issue #3163.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The existing human dendritic cell terms are modeled using marker phenotype restrictions. CD14-negative status is represented logically with `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`) and `PR_000001350` for CD14, matching existing ontology patterns for absent surface markers. The change was limited to the two terms explicitly requested and supported by the issue discussion.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Reviewed imported issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked the existing term blocks for `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`.\n+- Checked the existing marker expression and lacking-expression ontology pattern.\n+- Verified the supplied PMIDs correspond to OMIP immunophenotyping references.\n+- Preserved existing references and added the requested references.\n+- Avoided modifying the broader `CL_0001056` term.\n+- Validated ontology functional syntax with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`.\n+- Checked the diff for whitespace errors with `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+- `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`: passed\n+- `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`: passed\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"ISSUE_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+Changes committed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+I updated the two requested human dendritic cell terms, `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`, to include CD14-negative status. I did not apply this to the broader `CL_0001056` human dendritic cell term, consistent with the maintainer note that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md","relativePath":"PR_COMMENTS.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n===================================================================\n--- /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n+++ /__w/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/PR_COMMENTS.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@\n+## Summary\n+\n+This PR addresses issue #3163 by adding CD14-negative characterization to the two requested human dendritic cell terms:\n+\n+- `CL_0001057` myeloid dendritic cell, human\n+- `CL_0001058` plasmacytoid dendritic cell, human\n+\n+The broader `CL_0001056` dendritic cell, human term was intentionally left unchanged because the issue discussion notes that some human dendritic cells can express CD14.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001057` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Updated the textual definition for `CL_0001058` to include `CD14-negative`.\n+- Added the requested OMIP references as additional definition xrefs without removing the existing `PMID:22343568` reference:\n+  - `PMID:34260151`\n+  - `PMID:36470845`\n+  - `PMID:37254600`\n+  - `PMID:38343094`\n+  - `PMID:40095400`\n+- Added logical axioms using the existing Cell Ontology pattern for lacking a plasma membrane part:\n+  - `CL_4030046 some PR_000001350` for CD14-negative status\n+- Added issue tracker annotations linking both updated terms to issue #3163.\n+\n+## Rationale\n+\n+The existing human dendritic cell terms are modeled using marker phenotype restrictions. CD14-negative status is represented logically with `CL_4030046` (`lacks_plasma_membrane_part`) and `PR_000001350` for CD14, matching existing ontology patterns for absent surface markers. The change was limited to the two terms explicitly requested and supported by the issue discussion.\n+\n+## Checklist\n+\n+- Reviewed imported issue title, body, and comments.\n+- Checked the existing term blocks for `CL_0001057` and `CL_0001058`.\n+- Checked the existing marker expression and lacking-expression ontology pattern.\n+- Verified the supplied PMIDs correspond to OMIP immunophenotyping references.\n+- Preserved existing references and added the requested references.\n+- Avoided modifying the broader `CL_0001056` term.\n+- Validated ontology functional syntax with `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`.\n+- Checked the diff for whitespace errors with `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+- `git diff --check -- src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`: passed\n+- `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/opencode/cl-edit-check.owl`: passed\n","additions":42,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","time":{"start":1778975886728,"end":1778975886743}},"id":"prt_e3339994b0012ZPWCQqF0NfjCJ","sessionID":"ses_1ccc91ca1ffeAz0tVsMxSuhbjd","messageID":"msg_e333982f0001Grj1kQv4knwlln"}}
